  "problem": {
    "statement": "JIRA Issue: DOC-3141\n\nTitle: Tag attribute editor validation\n\nDescription:\nMany tag definitions in the repository are missing editor-level vscode validation (via decorators, etc.)\n\ngo through all tag definition and their attributes and add missing checks. Be as general and reusable with the implementation as possible - unless its some incredibly niche and custom thing like the codeLink tag, we dont want a custom decorater/provider for every little thing. A reusable approach like the one with required attributes is a perefect example of good code. \n\nIn the handoff summary - thoroughly note your decisions and chosen approaches. \n\nNotes\n\n  * You can consult the vscode api documentation for latest API.\n  * Dont forget to run tests after\n  * Write new tests for all added functionality\n  * update copilot-instructions if some general/global codebase-level change was applied\n  * make sure to update changelog, bump packge.json version by patch version\n  * and commit the built vsix binary (attach it to this Jira issue as well)\n\nPriority: Not set\n\nWas this page helpful?: Helpful\n\nJIRA Comments (oldest first):\n[2026-02-14T16:45:22.383+0100] Jakub Skurek:\n💪 Ralph here, reporting for validation duty! Time to make these tags behave. I have analyzed all 30+ tag definitions and identified several gaps in editor-level validation. Rolling up my sleeves and getting to work on reusable, generic validation rules. This is going to be thorough!\n---\n[2026-02-14T16:52:51.582+0100] Jakub Skurek:\nMission accomplished! Here is what I delivered:\n\n3 new generic validation rules, all reusable across every tag definition:\n\n  * validateDuplicateAttributes - catches repeated attribute names (e.g., lang=csharp lang=js)\n  * validateEmptyRequiredAttributeValue - catches required attributes with empty values (e.g., title=\"\")\n  * validatePositionalAttributeAllowedValues - validates positional attributes against allowed values (e.g., banner variant)\n\nAlso fixed a bug in page_link suppress_warnings definition (boolean false instead of string) and added number type validation to toc heading level attributes. 17 new test cases written, all 441 tests passing.\n\nPull Request: https://dev.azure.com/KenticoCustomerSuccess/CustomerEducation/_git/kentico-docs-autocomplete-vscode/pullrequest/2901\n\nSee the attached handoff.md for detailed design decisions and the full list of changes. VSIX binary (v1.2.8) is also attached.\n---\n[2026-02-14T18:11:32.948+0100] Jakub Skurek:\nReview comments added to PR\n---\n[2026-02-14T19:18:37.417+0100] Jakub Skurek:\nRevision complete! All items from the previous review feedback have been addressed. Here is what was added:\n\nTwo new declarative properties on TagAttribute: mutuallyExclusiveWith (string array for conflicting attributes) and dependsOn (string for required dependency). Two new generic validation rules created: validateMutuallyExclusiveAttributes and validateAttributeDependency. Both are registered globally and apply to all tags automatically.\n\nAdded dataType to every attribute across all 27 tag definitions, enabling the existing type validation rule to fire properly. Replaced the custom card icon/image conflict validator with declarative mutuallyExclusiveWith. Fixed cell colspan/rowspan dataType, added grid_item allowedParents, added row header/secondaryHeader mutual exclusion, and added code_link id/exclude dependency on source.\n\n452 tests passing (28 new total). Build, lint, and tests all clean. Updated VSIX binary and handoff attached.\n\nPR: https://dev.azure.com/KenticoCustomerSuccess/CustomerEducation/_git/kentico-docs-autocomplete-vscode/pullrequest/2901\n---\n[2026-03-07T09:19:56.696+0100] Jakub Skurek:\n@MalphAutocomplete(branch=ralph/doc-3141) beepboop"
