      "description": "Sends input to the specified command or Bash session.\n* This tool can be used to send input to a running Bash command or an interactive console app.\n* Bash commands are run in an interactive Bash session with a TTY device and Bash command processor.\n* shellId (required) must match the shellId used to invoke the async bash command.\n* You can send text, {up}, {down}, {left}, {right}, {enter}, and {backspace} as input.\n* Some applications present a list of options to select from. The selection is often denoted using ❯, >, or different formatting.\n* When presented with a list of items, make a selection by sending arrow keys like {up} or {down} to move the selection to your chosen item and then {enter} to select it.\n* The response will contain any output read after \"delay\" seconds. Delay should be appropriate for the task and never less than 10 seconds.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "shellId": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Indicates which Bash session to run the command in. Multiple sessions may be used to run different commands at the same time."
