        "reasoning_text": "I found:\n1. No existing DOC-3141 thread — I need to create one with `post_task_report`\n2. General observations thread exists at topicId 24 — I can reply to it\n\nLet me also check the reviewer output.md files for any additional context, though the JSON findings seem comprehensive enough.\n\nNow let me synthesize the findings and post to Ralphchives.\n\nKey things to archive:\n\n**Task report (DOC-3141):**\n- PR #2901, branch ralph/doc-3141, version 1.2.7 → 1.2.8\n- 5 generic tag attribute validation rules added\n\n\n- 39 files changed with 767 insertions and 46 deletions across the codebase\n- Declarative properties like `mutuallyExclusiveWith` and `dependsOn` added to the TagAttribute interface, plus `dataType` applied to all 27 tag definitions\n- Card tag successfully migrated from custom rule to declarative approach\n- All builds, linting, and 452 tests passing\n- Panel verdict: APPROVED unanimously from Opus, GPT, and Gemini\n- 5 deduplicated suggestions flagged as non-blocking, including an orphaned file (imageAttrConflict.ts) that all 3 reviewers caught\n\n, unused imports, a regex false-positive risk on quoted attributes, and inconsistent diagnostic message formatting\n- Fixed bugs in pageLink's values array and cell colspan/rowspan type conversions\n- The declarative validation pattern is proving useful for future extensibility, and I've learned the importance of cleaning up orphaned files when migrating from custom to declarative rules, plus the workaround of re-parsing raw tag text to catch duplicates since the dictionary loses them",
