            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "ralphchives-write-post_task_report",
              "arguments": "{\"title\": \"DOC-3141: Tag attribute editor validation — review\", \"content\": \"## What was reviewed\\n\\nPR #2901 (`ralph/doc-3141` → `main`, version 1.2.7 → 1.2.8) adds **5 generic, reusable tag attribute validation rules** and extends the `TagAttribute` interface with two declarative properties. 39 files changed (767 ins, 46 del), 452 tests passing.\\n\\n### The 5 new rules (all in `src/logic/diagnostics/tags/rules/`)\\n1. **validateDuplicateAttributes** — regex-based detection on raw tag text (dictionary would lose dupes)\\n2. **validateEmptyRequiredAttributeValue** — handles both positional (argv1) and named attrs\\n3. **validateMutuallyExclusiveAttributes** — driven by `mutuallyExclusiveWith` property, deduplicates pairs\\n4. **validateAttributeDependency** — driven by `dependsOn` property\\n5. **validatePositionalAttributeAllowedValues** — validates positional values against allowed list\\n\\nAll rules follow `TagValidationRuleFn` signature, use `createTagDiagnostic` helper, skip closing tags, and are registered in `rulesRegister.ts`.\\n\\n### Declarative properties pattern\\nTwo new optional properties on `TagAttribute` in `types.ts`:\\n- `mutuallyExclusiveWith: string[]` — declares which attrs conflict (e.g., card icon vs image)\\n- `dependsOn: string` — declares a required parent attr (e.g., codeLink id/exclude depend on source)\\n\\nThis replaces per-tag custom validation functions with data-driven rules. The card tag's `validateCardIconImageConflict` was migrated to this approach as proof of concept.\\n\\n### Also in this PR\\n- `dataType` (from `AttributeDataType` enum) added to all attributes across all 27 tag definitions\\n- **Bugfix**: pageLink `suppress_warnings` had `values: ['true', false]` (unquoted boolean) → fixed to `['true', 'false']`\\n- **Bugfix**: cell `colspan`/`rowspan` dataType corrected from `String` to `Number`\\n- gridItem gained `allowedParents: [TagNames.GRID]`\\n\\n## Panel verdict\\n\\n**APPROVED** (unanimous — Opus, GPT, Gemini). 5 deduplicated non-blocking suggestions, 0 critical, 0 style.\\n\\n### Key findings (deduplicated across 3 reviewers)\\n\\n| # | Finding | Flagged by |\\n|---|---------|-----------|\\n| 1 | **Orphaned file** `card/diagnostics/imageAttrConflict.ts` — import removed but file not deleted | All 3 |\\n| 2 | **Unused imports** — `findTagAttributeNameRange` imported but unused in validateDuplicateAttributes | GPT, Gemini |\\n| 3 | **Unused type imports** — `TagValidationContext` imported but only `TagValidationRuleFn` used (3 files) | Opus |\\n| 4 | **Regex false-positive risk** — duplicate-detection regex `/\\\\b([\\\\w-]+)\\\\s*(?=\\\\s*=)/gi` can match inside quoted attr values (e.g., `title=\\\"lang=test\\\"` would false-match `lang`) | GPT, Gemini |\\n| 5 | **Inconsistent diagnostic message** — positional attrs say \\\"Required src has an empty value\\\" vs named attrs say \\\"Required attribute 'title' has an empty value\\\" | GPT |\\n\\n## Gotchas for future work\\n\\n- **Orphaned files on declarative migration**: When replacing a custom validation rule with declarative properties, remember to delete the old rule file — lint won't catch it since nothing imports it anymore.\\n- **Duplicate detection requires raw text**: `tagInstance.attributes` is a dictionary, so duplicate attribute names are silently merged. The validateDuplicateAttributes rule correctly re-parses raw tag text via regex for this reason.\\n- **codeLink retains custom rules**: Not all validation can be declarative — codeLink's source/section/exclude rules are content-aware and remain as per-tag `validationRules`.\", \"tags\": [\"DOC-3141\",\"DOC\",\"review\",\"validation\",\"malph\"]}"
